#. translators: %s: the IP address in the site's From address.
#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:200
#, php-format
msgid "Mail is sent from the IP address \"%s\" instead of a domain. SPF, DKIM and DMARC cannot be set up for an IP address, so most receiving servers reject mail from it. Set a real domain in the From address."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the domain part of the site's From address.
#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:217
#, php-format
msgid "Mail is sent from \"%s\", which is not a usable domain. Messages are rejected before they leave the server, and no amount of mail configuration will change that. Set a real domain in the From address."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the domain part of the site's From address.
#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:230
#, php-format
msgid "Mail is sent from the domain \"%s\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:243
msgid "SPF record"
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:257
msgid "No SPF record was found. Receiving servers have no way to tell which machines may send for this domain, so mail from it is widely treated as suspicious."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:267
msgid "The SPF record ends in \"+all\", which authorises every server on the internet to send as this domain. That is the same as publishing no policy, and some providers treat it as worse."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:288
msgid "An SPF record exists but does not end in \"-all\" or \"~all\", so it never says what to do about servers it has not listed. Receivers are left to guess."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:301
msgid "An SPF record is published and delegates its policy to another domain with \"redirect=\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:313
msgid "An SPF record is published and states a policy for unlisted servers."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:327
msgid "DKIM key"
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:347
msgid "This domain returns a DKIM record for every selector asked for, including one invented at random, so nothing can be concluded about which keys actually exist. A wildcard DNS record is the usual cause."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:371
msgid "No DKIM key was found at any of the selectors the common mail providers use. DNS cannot be asked to list selectors, so a key published under a name of your own would not be seen here. Without DKIM, nothing cryptographically ties a message to this domain."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: comma-separated list of DKIM selector names.
#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:385
#, php-format
msgid "A DKIM key is published at the selector \"%s\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:416
msgid "DMARC policy"
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:430
msgid "No DMARC policy was found. Gmail and Yahoo now require one from anyone sending them bulk mail, and without it SPF and DKIM failures carry no stated consequence."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:440
msgid "A DMARC policy is published but set to \"p=none\", which only asks for reports and tells receivers to take no action. That is a reasonable place to start and a poor place to stay."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:452
msgid "A DMARC policy is published and asks receivers to act on failures."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:473
msgid "Skipped, because the site has no usable sending domain to look up."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/DomainAuth.php:483
msgid "This server does not allow PHP to look up DNS records, so the check could not run. This is not the same as the record being missing."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: name of the plugin, theme or code, 2: file path.
#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:138
#, php-format
msgid "wp_mail() is defined by %1$s (%2$s) instead of WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:144
msgid "A replacement does not have to run pre_wp_mail or phpmailer_init, so the route chosen in Mail Vitals may never be used, and failures may never reach the send log."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:145
msgid "A replacement does not have to report what happened, so messages it sends or fails to send may be missing from the send log."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: name of the callback, such as __return_false.
#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:156
#, php-format
msgid "A callback that always stops sending, %s, is attached to pre_wp_mail, so no mail leaves this site. This is a common way to switch mail off on a staging site. If that was intended, nothing needs to change; if it was not, this is why mail is not being sent."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: priority Mail Vitals takes over sending at.
#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:165
#, php-format
msgid "Other code is attached to pre_wp_mail. A callback there that returns anything other than null decides what wp_mail() returns: at a priority below %d it stops the message before Mail Vitals sees it, and otherwise it also runs inside each of Mail Vitals' own attempts, where it can take the message over in place of the route."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:168
msgid "Other code is attached to pre_wp_mail. When a callback there returns anything other than null, wp_mail() stops and returns that value without reporting success or failure, so those messages do not appear in the send log."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: priority Mail Vitals configures SMTP at.
#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:175
#, php-format
msgid "Other code is attached to phpmailer_init. A callback that runs after Mail Vitals' (priority %d) can overwrite the SMTP server, port and login it set, so mail leaves through a server other than the one configured here."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:178
msgid "Other code configures the mailer through phpmailer_init. Mail Vitals is leaving sending to WordPress, so this is not a conflict; it is listed so you know what is shaping outgoing mail."
msgstr ""

#: src/Diagnostics/MailInterference.php:182
msgid "No other code is attached to the hooks that send mail, and wp_mail() is WordPress's own."
msgstr ""

